From 2d147cd1274bf1cb3bfb89879e93627e052e3124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wasm64 port <wasm64@localhost>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:11:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm64 port: build against the QED64 Lean fork (4.33.0-pre)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two one-line source changes; everything else the v4.7.0-era game needs
is supplied by the build's compat tree (the `Mathlib.Tactic` umbrella
that Game/Metadata.lean imports is provided under its real module name
by wasm/compat/Mathlib/Tactic.lean, so the import is untouched):

- Game.lean: `Languages "English"` -> `Languages "en"` (the client
  matches ISO codes; "English" matched no UI language).
- Game/Levels/OrIntro/L02.lean: bind `K` explicitly,
  `Statement (K O S : Prop)`. Under v4.7.0 the `K` of the goal `K ∨ S`
  was an auto-bound implicit; this GameServer's `Statement` elaborator
  no longer auto-binds signature identifiers ("Unknown identifier `K`").
  Auto-bound implicits were placed first, so the player's object list
  (`K O S : Prop`) is unchanged.

All 103 reachable modules compile with -Dlinter.all=false
-Dtactic.hygienic=false -Dlinter.unusedVariables.funArgs=true; MakeGame
emits the full 10-world / 88-level gamedata.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Game.lean                    | 2 +-
 Game/Levels/OrIntro/L02.lean | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Game.lean b/Game.lean
index a28af4b..717eca7 100755
--- a/Game.lean
+++ b/Game.lean
@@ -174,7 +174,7 @@ Warning: In most browsers, deleting cookies will also clear the local storage
 "
 
 /-! Information to be displayed on the servers landing page. -/
-Languages "English"
+Languages "en"
 CaptionShort "Lean intro to Logic"
 CaptionLong "A mostly self-contained introduction to constructive logic using Lean. Learn how each propositional connective can be introduced and eliminated using both terms and tactics."
 CoverImage "images/logic0101_v4.png"
diff --git a/Game/Levels/OrIntro/L02.lean b/Game/Levels/OrIntro/L02.lean
index 2d75a68..f71dbc8 100755
--- a/Game/Levels/OrIntro/L02.lean
+++ b/Game/Levels/OrIntro/L02.lean
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ You've just unlocked `or_inr`. It turns evidence for the righthand of an `∨` p
 "
 
 /-- Or Introduction Right -/
-Statement (O S : Prop)(s : S) : K ∨ S := by
+Statement (K O S : Prop)(s : S) : K ∨ S := by
   exact or_inr s
 
 Conclusion "
